Removal of members.– The Governor on his own volition or on the
recommendation of the District Public Safety Commission may remove a member
from office if he–
(a)
ceases to be a citizen of Pakistan;
(b)
is found suffering from physical or mental incapacity or illness;
(c)
is guilty of misconduct;
(d)
is found to have dealt with any matter in which he had a conflict of
interest;
(e)
is convicted of a criminal offence;
(f)
is declared a bankrupt, loan defaulter or tax evader;
(g)
is involved in activities prejudicial to the ideology, interest, security,
unity, solidarity, peace and integrity of Pakistan and its people, and the
good order and harmony of society;
(h)
brings the District Public Safety Commission into disrepute;
(i)
fails to attend its three consecutive meetings without any reasonable
cause.

